api v5.1.0 deploy left the service unhealthy in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of about 18%. Rolled back to v5.0.0, the most recent release marked healthy in production. The rollback reached all regions. Next: confirm the error rate recovers and find the root cause in v5.1.0.", "idempotency_key": "payments-api-v5.1.0-rollback-sev2", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01TYLM1uhQd3VP53o8ZLJJJb", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-api", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled payments-api back to v5.0.0 and opened a SEV2 incident. The error rate has dropped from 18% to 0.2%.\n\n- **Which service:** There's no service called \"payments\", so I tried likely names and found payments-api. It was running this morning's release, v5.1.0, in all three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). It was failing with an 18% error rate, and v5.1.0 is listed as degraded. I only checked the service names I could guess, so if there are other payments services, I haven't looked at them.\n- **Rollback:** v5.0.0 is the most recent release marked healthy in production. It's now live in all three regions, and payments-api reports healthy. Since v5.0.0 has been healthy in production before, change-manager approval wasn't needed.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 (SEV2) is open for payments-api, and on-call has been paged. The summary describes the v5.1.0 errors and the rollback. Next steps are to keep an eye on stability and find what broke in v5.1.0 before anyone redeploys it.", "type": "text"}]}]}